5-c23a-5f79-bdef-25f46f0b96dc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-180748"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-183519"] :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined as\n\n$$\nA={{n}^{2}+2n:n\\in N,\\,n\\ge 2}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following sets is equivalent to $A?$" :question/worked-solution "The condition after the \"$:$\" symbol\n\n$$\nn\\in N,\\,n\\ge 2\n$$\n\nstates that $n$ can be any natural number that satisfies the inequality $n\\ge 2.$ In other words, \n\n$$\nn={2,3,4,5,…}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elements of $A$ are all the terms of the sequence ${a}_{n},$ given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={n}^{2}+2n,\\,n\\in {2,3,4,5,…}.\n$$\n\nLet's write down the first few terms of our sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & ={2}^{2}+2(2)=4+4=8 \\\\ {a}_{3} & ={3}^{2}+2(3)=9+6=15 \\\\ {a}_{4} & ={4}^{2}+2(4)=16+8=24 \\\\ {a}_{5} & ={5}^{2}+2(5)=25+10=35 \\\\  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nA={8,15,24,35,…}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-180746/selection/6b5336f350283315fa83db10aac53d2f1be55c39a5ac6013b53d9bf5ee488598" :answer/id #uuid "4cf70aaa-046a-59ee-84ac-1864570554a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\frac{1}{4},\\frac{1}{5},\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-180746/selection/c33d15e71b94b91a5b97c401a8c4253c8dfe16603cff634f99379e87456bc3ec" :answer/id #uuid "8c88d92e-2975-5e24-a001-514444890ff1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\frac{1}{3},\\frac{1}{5},\\frac{1}{7},\\frac{1}{4}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-180746/selection/ad8397872f9724115e8c2d68b6ef62cdeecf442baa4ba31fefc96964ebd6c46b" :answer/id #uuid "3edd16d4-7b98-585d-8cb9-78fa7e62dbde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\frac{1}{4},\\frac{1}{5},\\frac{1}{6},\\frac{1}{7}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-180746/selection/572ff276b427f1ca11318fcc4150eb2dd7c1bab6c5c9baa54e21f941bdc699b0" :answe