={{b}_{n}\\,:\\,{b}_{n+1}={b}_{n}+5\\,,\\,{b}_{1}=2,\\,n\\in N}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following sets is equivalent to $B?$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of $B$ are all the terms of the *recursive* sequence ${b}_{n},$ given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n+1}={b}_{n}+5,\\,{b}_{1}=2,\\,n\\in N.\n$$\n\nLet's write down the first few terms of our sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & =2 \\\\ {b}_{2} & ={b}_{1}+5 \\\\  & =2+5 \\\\  & =7 \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={b}_{2}+5 \\\\  & =7+5 \\\\  & =12 \\\\ {b}_{4} & ={b}_{3}+5 \\\\  & =12+5 \\\\  & =17 \\\\  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nB={2,7,12,17,…}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-183670/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e28c42e-0d82-5e82-a130-a2cb72fb96d1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-183670"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-183672/selection/b925cd29734804578a1a8feadada0a725f8fe6e7158a5c7b1a0d2278f6cb9019" :answer/id #uuid "cd69eaf1-ac97-57ab-8e25-33cd90e723d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{1,4,7,19,40,64,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183672/selection/71998027741627b7dbf18414ac5d1b32ccff20676c938da3dcf925381fb5d310" :answer/id #uuid "da6f27bd-6eeb-5ac8-b8c8-8312c45071b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{1,4,7,14,28,35,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183672/selection/ab58e30aaf0af280ebe90d57c3d739e4fd80fea94229ad80f4ab8541c10d7874" :answer/id #uuid "d7a1ad6d-e5bd-5ba6-871a-d5f9485fa142" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{1,4,7,19,28,63,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183672/selection/b11350f74ba64f0f82478a4eec3f9fd0722277443618b7c6d8c71929fc5a996b" :answer/id #uuid "d2f4f20b-5a6a-530c-9c06-f24d708301da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{1,4,7,19,40,97,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183672/selection/d71a4c3a920d70b06be1b2798601b49b71ca137d10f3273aec275fa644aed8f0" :answer/id #uuid "a2e0e804-a681-5f83-9886-d513569e58a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{1,4,7,14,21,28,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183672/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "15a76e78-f0df-5a5f-825d-577a01fd6d85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-183672/selection/b11350f74ba64f0f82478a4eec3f9fd0722277443618b7c6d8c71929fc5a996b" :answer-field/choices ["q-183672/selection/b925cd29734804578a1a8feadada0a725f8fe6e7158a5c7b1a0d2278f6cb9019" "q-183672/selection/71998027741627b7dbf18414ac5d1b32ccff20676c938da3dcf925381fb5d310" "q-183672/selection/ab58e30aaf0af280ebe90d57c3d739e4fd80fea94229ad80f4ab8541c10d7874" "q-183672/selection/b11350f74ba64f0f82478a4eec3f9fd0722277443618b7c6d8c71929fc5a996b" "q-183672/selection/d71a4c3a920d70b06be1b2798601b49b71ca137d10f3273aec275fa644aed8f0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-183672" :question/id #uuid "72ac262e-0f23-52d4-8743-dab235958f32" :question/math-academy-id "q-183672" :question/problem "Consider the set $B,$ defined as\n\n$$\nB={{b}_{n}\\,:\\,{b}_{n+2}={b}_{n+1}+3{b}_{n}\\,,\\,{b}_{1}=1,\\,{b}_{2}=4,\\,n\\in N}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following sets is equivalent to $B?$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of $B$ are all the terms of the *recursive* sequence ${b}_{n},$ given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n+2}={b}_{n+1}+3{b}_{n},\\,{b}_{1}=1,\\,{b}_{2}=4,\\,n\\in N.\n$$\n\nLet's write down the first few terms of our sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & =1 \\\\ {b}_{2} & =4 \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={b}_{2}+3{b}_{1} \\\\  & =4+3(1) \\\\  & =7 \\\\ {b}_{4} & ={b}_{3}+3{b}_{2} \\\\  & =7+3(4) \\\\  & =19 \\\\ {b}_{5} & ={b}_{4}+3{b}_{3} \\\\  & =19+3(7) \\\\  & =40 \\\\ {b}_{6} & ={b}_{5}+3{b}_{4} \\\\  & =40+3(19) \\\\  & =97 \\\\  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nB={1,4,7,19,40,97,…}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-183672/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e28c42e-0d82-5e82-a130-a2cb72fb96d1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-183672"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-181705/selection/9cc63b95c31111b0c14d8ae1b1bef448964e6201d82a7cdf105908f491a54a04" :answer/id #uuid "f658838f-5020-5f6d-9be7-30b8d69d0330" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{2,6,18,58,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181705/selection/392ca646d9bbfc4d34da0588f47eb67d2418e6312fc7213b23becb50327cf1e3" :answer/id #uuid "87622484-f3e3-5473-a331-58a2189bff6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{2,6,18,32,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181705/selection/147d2f13adb44c6c9313883e797b24af7307ad0b13dac185fc369dcfd7f9df31" :answer/id #uuid "9a753427-570e-5a29-b4d4-7cb36920644e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{2,6,18,54,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181705/selection/6796be0b2855c815402535507f18914e9e94f54ee6576c9a2120aa922184f115" :answer/id #uuid "d1c8cfae-faa2-5d69-b8d3-0d7157059a90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{2,6,18,22,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181705/selection/3c7ebb9785c4e6f05e1a44e4a1c8b3084ad15d6dd6d76b08f07eba9886d39354" :answer/id #uuid "c21e5797-8626-5134-9cb5-0a8535de5409" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{2,6,18,24,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181705/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f701ce55-13f7-5e09-9270-5d0343c143fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-181705/selection/147d2f13adb44c6c9313883e797b24af7307ad0b13dac185fc369dcfd7f9df31" :answer-field/choices ["q-181705/selection/9cc63b95c31111b0c14d8ae1b1bef448964e6201d82a7cdf105908f491a54a04" "q-181705/selection/392ca646d9bbfc4d34da0588f47eb67d2418e6312fc7213b23becb50327cf1e3" "q-181705/selection/147d2f13adb44c6c9313883e797b24af7307ad0b13dac185fc369dcfd7f9df31" "q-181705/selection/6796be0b2855c815402535507f18914e9e94f54ee6576c9a2120aa922184f115" "q-181705/selection/3c7ebb9785c4e6f05e1a44e4a1c8b3084ad15d6dd6d76b08f07eba9886d39354"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-181705" :question/id #uuid "1011d810-7a37-5d41-acb5-43acec278417" :question/math-academy-id "q-181705" :question/problem "Consider the set $B,$ defined as\n\n$$\nB={{b}_{n}\\,:\\,{b}_{n+1}=3{b}_{n}\\,,\\,{b}_{1}=2,\\,n\\in N}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following sets is equivalent to $B?$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of $B$ are all the terms of the *recursive* sequence ${b}_{n},$ given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n+1}=3{b}_{n},\\,{b}_{1}=2,\\,n\\in N.\n$$\n\nLet's write down the first few terms of our sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & =2 \\\\ {b}_{2} & =3{b}_{1} \\\\  & =3(2) \\\\  & =6 \\\\ {b}_{3} & =3{b}_{2} \\\\  & =3(6) \\\\  & =18 \\\\ {b}_{4} & =3{b}_{3} \\\\  & =3(18) \\\\  & =54 \\\\  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nB={2,6,18,54,…}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-181705/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e28c42e-0d82-5e82-a130-a2cb72fb96d1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-181705"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-13177"] :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined as\n\n$$\nA = \\{ (-1)^n \\, n : n \\in \\mathbb{N} \\}.\n$$\n\nWrite down a set that's equivalent to $A$ using ellipsis notation." :question/worked-solution "The elements of $A$ are all the terms of the sequence $a_n,$ given by\n\n$$\na_n = (-1)^n \\,n, \\qquad n \\in \\mathbb N = \\{1,2,3,4,\\ldots\\}.\n$$\n\nLet's write down the first few terms of our sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =(-1)^{1}(1)=-1 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =(-1)^{2}(2)=2 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =(-1)^{3}(3)=-3 \\\\ {a}_{4} & =(-1)^{4}(4)=4 \\\\  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nA = \\{ -1, 2, -3, 4,  \\ldots \\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-13142"] :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined as\n\n$$\nA = \\left \\{ 4^n : n \\in \\mathbb Z,\\, -2\\leq n\\leq 2  \\right \\}.\n$$\n\nDescribe $A$ by listing all of its elements." :question/worked-solution "The condition after the \"$:$\" symbol, \n\n$$\nn \\in \\mathbb Z,\\, -2\\leq n\\leq 2\n$$\n\nstates that $n$ can be any integer that satisfies the inequality $-2\\leq n\\leq 2.$ \n\nTherefore, the elements of $A$ are all the terms of the sequence $a_n,$ given by\n\n$$\na_n = 4^n, \\qquad n \\in \\{0, \\pm 1, \\pm 2\\}.\n$$\n\nLet's write down all the terms of our sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{-2} & ={4}^{-2}=\\frac{1}{16} \\\\ {a}_{-1} & ={4}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {a}_{0} & ={4}^{0}=1 \\\\ {a}_{1} & ={4}^{1}=4 \\\\ {a}_{2} & ={4}^{2}=16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nA = \\left\\{\\dfrac{1}{16},\\,\\dfrac{1}{4},\\,1,\\,4,\\,16 \\right\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-13285"] :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined as\n\n$$\nA = \\big \\{ a_n \\,:\\,a_{n+1} = 2a_{n} - 1, \\, a_1 = 2,\\, n \\in \\mathbb N \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nWrite down a set that's equivalent to $A$ using ellipsis notation." :question/worked-solution "The elements of $A$ are all the terms of the *recursive* sequence $a_n,$ given by\n\n$$\na_{n+1} =2a_{n} - 1, \\quad a_1 =2,\\qquad n \\in \\mathbb N.\n$$\n\nLet's write down the first few terms of our sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =2 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =2{a}_{1}-1 \\\\  & =2(2)-1 \\\\  & =3 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =2{a}_{2}-1 \\\\  & =2(3)-1 \\\\  & =5 \\\\ {a}_{4} & =2{a}_{3}-1 \\\\  & =2(5)-1 \\\\  & =9 \\\\ {a}_{5} & =2{a}_{4}-1 \\\\  & =2(9)-1 \\\\  & =17 \\\\  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nA = \\left\\{2,3,5,9,17,\\ldots \\right\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
